  "id": "COMPOUND:39816 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "Streptenol C is implicated in the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in epigenetic control of gene expression. This complex is targeted by multiple compounds, including Hyrtioreticulin D, Docosanoic acid, pentyl ester, and (2S-trans)-6-(2-Chloroethyl)-2,3-dihydro-3-hydroxy-2,5,7-trimethyl-1H-inden-1-one, all of which ultimately direct their activity to SN12K1. The consistent evidence across these three paths suggests a mechanistic link between Streptenol C and SN12K1, where the compound modulates the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn affects SN12K1. The shared target of these compounds at the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex indicates a potential common pathway, though the exact mechanism by which Streptenol C influences this complex remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible, biologically relevant relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Streptenol C in this process.",
